." Manual page for aero-telemetry
.TH AERO-TELEMETRY 1 "November 2026" "Aero Linux v1.4.0" "Aero Linux Manual"
.SH NAME
aero-telemetry \- High-frequency kernel and system performance telemetry daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aero-telemetry
[B\-\-daemonR] [B\-\-intervalR IMSecR] [B\-\-exportR IFormatR] [B\-\-helpR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aero-telemetry
is a low-overhead system telemetry service engineered for the Aero Linux operating system.
It aggregates hardware performance counters, CPU thermal metrics, eBPF probe statistics,
and memory bus utilization into a compact binary circular ring buffer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run the telemetry collector in the background as an unprivileged daemon.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " IMSecR
Sampling frequency in milliseconds (default: 250ms).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-export " " IFormatR
Output format for diagnostic dumps: json, prometheus, or binary (default: json).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print telemetry service version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display brief usage synopsis and available options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AERO_TELEMETRY_LOG
Path to the operational event log (default: /var/log/aero/telemetry.log).
.SH AUTHORS
Written and engineered by Ronit Gupta (@ronitgupta138) for Aero Linux.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aero (1),
.BR aero-profile (1)
